Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** for `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10.0
**Calibration:** Class is tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]` — integration-test rules applied throughout.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**Smell:** Control flow (`if`/`else`) inside a test method changes which assertion runs. One branch may never execute, hiding a testing gap.

**Affected test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 96)

```csharp
// SMELL — branching means one path is never verified
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = CreatePremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** The `PremiumUser` branch is never exercised unless specific data triggers it — a hidden gap in coverage.

---

### ❷ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**Smell:** Test executes production code but contains zero assertions. MSTest reports it as passing even if every insert silently corrupts data.

**Affected test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
// SMELL — no assertion; "passes" even if inserts silently fail
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix — verify the side-effect:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — this test inflates the pass count while verifying nothing.

---

### ❸ Sleepy Test — MEDIUM *(downgraded from High; integration calibration)*

**Smell:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces a hard 3-second wall-clock wait. Even in integration tests this causes non-deterministic timing and slows the suite.

**Affected test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
// SMELL — hard sleep; brittle on slow CI, wastes time on fast machines
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — use a polling retry loop with a timeout:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5),
        interval: TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(200));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within the timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures when the environment is slow; wasted wall-clock time when it's fast.

---

### ❹ Assertion Roulette — MEDIUM

**Smell:** Multiple assertions in one method with no failure messages. When one fails, the MSTest output shows `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no hint of *which* property was wrong.

**Affected test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28) — 4 message-less assertions

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add discriminating messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Time wasted diagnosing failures — you must read the source to find out which property failed.

---

## Smells Scanned — No Findings (15/19 clean)

| Smell | Result | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite is hermetic — no external resource dependency |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods (integration calibration also applies) |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions match items just inserted — self-documenting |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Each test targets distinct behavior |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]`, not a constructor |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is descriptive |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` calls |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB created fresh per test |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All methods contain statements |

---

## Well-Written Tests Worth Noting

- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — clean arrange-act-assert, single concern, clear assertion.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — good use of `Task.WhenAll` for concurrency testing with a concrete count assertion.
- **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — `CollectionAssert.AllItemsAreNotNull` is a strong secondary assertion.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| **1** | Assertion-Free Test (`BulkInsert`) | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after the loop | 2 min |
| **2** | Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | Split into two focused test methods | 10 min |
| **3** | Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert`) | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-until helper | 15 min |
| **4** | Assertion Roulette (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`) | Add message strings to each `Assert` call | 2 min |

Items 1 and 4 are quick wins you can ship today. Items 2 and 3 require a small refactor but eliminate the two most dangerous failure modes: hidden coverage gaps and CI flakiness.
